==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Excrescence}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|excrescens|excrēscēns}}, present participle of {{m|la|excresco|excrēscō}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something growing, usually abnormally, out of something else.
# {{label|en|phonetics}} A sound in a word without [[etymological]] reason.
#: ''"B" in "nimble" is an '''excrescent'''.''

====Related terms====
* [[excrescence]]

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Growing out in an abnormal or morbid manner or as a superfluity.
#* Alexander Pope
#*: Expunge the whole, or lop th' '''excrescent''' parts.

